  DOI: 10.37373/tekno.v14i1.2526  \n   Why it matters: Develops and evaluates a RAG-based chatbot specialized for academic information retrieval.\n\n3. \"HEAL-RAG: A Hybrid Evolving Retrieval-Augmented Generation Framework for Explainable Biomedical Data Analysis and Clinical Decision Support\"  \n   Publication Date: 2026-11-12  \n   First Author: Ronke Seyi Babatunde  \n   Venue: Algorithms  \n   DOI: 10.3390/a19110992  \n   Why it matters: Proposes a hybrid RAG framework aimed at explainable biomedical data analysis and clinical decision-making.\n\n4. \"Evaluating Embedding Models and Preprocessing for Retrieval of MDE Elements in RAG Systems\"  \n   Publication Date: 2026-11-12  \n   First Author: Julian Roßkothen  \n   Venue: KITopen (repository)  \n   DOI: 10.5445/ir/1000196452/pub  \n   Why it matters: Focuses on assessing embedding models and preprocessing steps critical for effective retrieval in RAG systems.\n\n5. \"An Explainable Semantic Enterprise Research Network for Institutional Collaboration Recommendation\"  \n   Publication Date: 2026-11-12  \n   First Author: Ameen Shaheen  \n   Venue: International Journal of Electronics and Communication Engineering  \n   DOI: 10.14445/23488549/ijece-v13i10p114  \n   Why it matters: Presents an explainable semantic network which may leverage retrieval-augmented methods for recommending institutional collaborations.\n\n6. \"AI ethics by design: implementing customizable guardrails for responsible AI development\"  \n   Publication Date: 2026-11-11  \n   First Author: Kristina Šekrst  \n   Venue: AI and Ethics  \n   DOI: 10.1007/s43681-026-01492-7  \n   Why it matters: Discusses ethics frameworks potentially relevant to RAG system design ensuring responsible use.\n\n7. \"Evaluating Prompting Frameworks for Enhancing ChatGPT-Assisted Literature Reviews and Ethical and Pedagogical Implications\"  \n   Publication Date: 2026-11-11  \n   First Author: Aminul Islam  \n   Venue: Trends in Higher Education  \n   DOI: 10.3390/higheredu5040133  \n   Why it matters: Evaluates prompting techniques which may advance the effectiveness of retrieval-augmented generation in literature review contexts.\n\nNote: 4 returned articles were skipped as they had been included in previous reports.","tools":[{"tool":"openalex_search_works","parameters":{"search":"retrieval augmented generation evaluation","filter":"from_publication_date:2026-10-01,type:article","sort":"publication_date:desc","per_page":10,"select":"id,doi,title,publication_date,cited_by_count,authorships,primary_location"},"output":{"_shortened":"[result shortened: every item is shown; fields left out: meta.notice (text), meta.x_query.oql (text), meta.x_query.x_new_oql (text), meta.x_query.oqo.get_rows (text), meta.x_query.order (text), meta.x_query.oqo.filter_rows[].{column_id (text), value (text), operator (text)}, meta.x_query.oqo.sort_by[].{column_id (text), direction (text)}, results[].authorships[].{author_position (text), author.observed_orcids (list), countries (list), raw_author_name (text), raw_affiliation_strings (list), raw_orcid (text)}, results[].authorships[].institutions[].{ror (text), country_code (text), lineage (list)}, results[].authorships[].affiliations[].{raw_affiliation_string (text), institution_ids (list)}, results[].{primary_location.is_oa (value), primary_location.landing_page_url (text), primary_location.pdf_url (value), primary_location.source.issn (list), primary_location.source.is_oa (value), primary_location.source.is_in_doaj (value), primary_location.source.is_core (value), primary_location.source.listed_in (list), primary_location.source.host_organization (text), primary_location.source.host_organization_name (text), primary_location.source.host_organization_lineage (list), primary_location.source.host_organization_lineage_names (list), primary_location.license (text), primary_location.license_id (text), primary_location.is_accepted (value), primary_location.is_published (value), primary_location.r